Revision history for PDL-Graphics-Cairo

(unreleased)
    - Driver::Cairo: text is rendered with grayscale antialiasing.
      $cr->set_antialias('gray') only covered shapes; Pango text followed
      fontconfig's rgba setting, so on Ubuntu 26.04 (rgba=rgb) saved images
      had red/blue subpixel fringes on text, and t/39 and t/41 failed
      (their colour-centroid measurement picked up the fringes).
    - Axes: get_xlim / get_ylim now return the range resolved by the last
      draw() (autoscale padding included, as in matplotlib) when no xlim/ylim
      is set. They used to return (0, 1) for autoscaled axes. Explicit limits
      are returned unchanged; (0, 1) only before the first draw.
    - Axes: image_frac_to_data / data_to_image_frac use the drawn range, so
      they match the image on autoscaled axes. The show_grid_scrub latency
      read-out was off by up to +/-19 ms at the edges of an autoscaled
      -100..600 ms axis (exact with an explicit xlim). (t/41,
      tools/verify_grid_scrub.pl section 7)
    - twinx / twiny: a twin of a figure()->axes() parent is registered with
      the Figure and drawn (it was silently dropped). Figure::add_axes is
      idempotent, so scripts that still call $fig->add_axes($twin) do not draw
      the twin twice; the examples no longer call it. (t/38)
    - twinx / twiny: the twin is drawn in the parent's final plot rectangle and
      shares its drawn range, so shared-axis data line up after tight_layout
      and subplots_adjust (the twin kept its creation-time geometry; the
      twinx right axis sat outside or inside the frame). twiny with an
      explicit parent xlim no longer dies. (t/39, t/26)
    - twinx / twiny: autoscale ranges of the parent and of the twin's own axis
      are re-resolved on every draw instead of freezing at the first one. (t/40)
    - tools/verify_gs3d.pl checks that the version lives only in
      PDL::Graphics::Cairo (no per-module $VERSION); 32/32.
    - Driver::GS show_grid_scrub: main_scrub => 1 selects the latency by a click
      or drag in the main window as well; panels flagged $ax->{_scrub_skip} get
      no latency line and are not click targets (t/43)
    - GridSpec: cell_margins — the same fixed margins for every Axes of the
      GridSpec, so all panels have the same plot area wherever they are in the
      grid and whichever cells are empty (0: the cell is the plot rectangle;
      a number; or a hash of sides). tight_layout(uniform_margins => 1) acts on
      subplot / subplots panels only and never reached add_gridspec panels:
      a 5x5 grid with 19 panels had plot areas of 128x64, 128x72, 116x90 and
      128x90 px. (t/44)
    - Figure: label_only($ax) and label_outer — tick numbers on chosen panels
      only / on the leftmost panel of each row and the lowest of each column,
      found from the panel positions so that grids with empty cells work. (t/44)
    - Axes: colorbar(cmap => ..., vmin => ..., vmax => ...) attaches a colorbar
      that does not come from a plot command (drawn on axis('off') panels too);
      reserve => 0 takes no room from the plot rectangle; tick_step puts the
      ticks at the multiples of a value. (t/44)
    - tight_layout: in a GridSpec cell narrower or lower than its margins the
      margins are shrunk so that a plot rectangle remains. They used to cross
      (a 25 px cell got a plot width of -22 px and data_to_pixel ran
      backwards). (t/44)
    - Driver::GS show_grid_scrub: each window is rendered as an image of its
      own current size. All windows used the size the driver was created with,
      so after a resize the figure was cut off at the right and bottom (window
      enlarged) or drawn small in the top-left corner (window shrunk), and the
      enlarged cell windows had the same fault from the start. (t/43)
    - Figure: add_connection — straight line between a point of one axes and a
      point of another (data / axes-fraction / figure-fraction coordinates, mixed
      per component), drawn over all axes; clf removes them (t/42)
    - Figure: add_text — text in the same coordinates as add_connection, drawn
      over all axes and unclipped (t/42)
    - Axes: data_to_pixel / axes_to_pixel (valid after draw), clip_pad_top
      (upper clip allowance of plotted data, default 15 px unchanged) (t/42)

0.3  2026-09-06
    - Driver::GS: show_grid_scrub — multi-window interactive scrub on giza-server:
      double-click a subplot opens a zoomed child window; drag places a latency
      marker and draws a vertical line at that latency in every parent subplot;
      the selection (marker + read-out) is kept after release and shared across
      all open child windows. macOS (Cocoa) giza-server only.
    - Interactive::Scrub: Cairo-free nearest-point / latency helper (t/36)
    - PGPLOT: multi-panel order follows the sign of NXSUB (>0 row-major default,
      <0 column-major); cpgsubp/cpgbeg/cpgpage/cpgpanl share one order (t/37)
    - Axes: image_frac_to_data / data_to_image_frac fall back to the autoscale
      range when no explicit xlim/ylim is set (fixes cursor->data mapping on
      auto-ranged axes)

0.2  2026-09-02
    - set_aspect('equal', $anchor): W/E/N/S anchoring (default C, unchanged)
    - axis('off') panels reserve no tick/label margin (tighter multi-panel layout)
    - colorbar reserved margin sized from actual bar/tick/label width (was fixed)
    - _colorbar_force: draw a colorbar on an axis('off') panel

0.1  2026-07-11
    - New plotting features since 0.01 (see t/08-t/32 for coverage):
        * contour (Marching Squares) alongside contourf
        * specgram (STFT spectrogram)
        * hexbin density plots
        * GridSpec / subplot_mosaic layouts; inset_axes
        * polar projection (PolarAxes)
        * pcolormesh (non-uniform quad mesh)
        * plot_date; scatter marker styles; grouped bar charts with yerr
        * style.use() presets + rcParams
        * minor ticks and tick_params
        * ListedColormap and Normalize variants (LogNorm / BoundaryNorm)
        * fill_between(where=) and fillstyle
        * twiny (twin y-axis), with label-rotation fixes
        * LTTB downsampling for large series
    - PDL::IO::PNG is now optional, not a hard dependency. Driver::Cairo
      previously did an unconditional `use PDL::IO::PNG qw(wpng)`, so the
      module failed to load on systems without it. It now loads PDL::IO::PNG
      lazily (our $HAVE_WPNG) and, when absent, writes PNG via Cairo's own
      write_to_png (~9.2ms vs ~3.4ms with wpng). This matches imread()'s
      existing PNG -> Image -> rpic fallback. Makefile.PL keeps it out of
      PREREQ_PM, lists it under runtime `recommends`, and prints a one-time
      advisory when it is not installed. New test t/07_png_fallback.t.
    - Driver unification: macOS native display is now the giza_server
      backend ('gs'). _default_backend() returns 'gs' on darwin (falling
      back to 'gnuplot' only when giza_server is neither running nor
      installed). Driver::GS->_available() added for that probe.
    - Driver::OSX / pdlcairo_viewer are DEPRECATED. They are no longer
      built or installed (Makefile.PL postamble/EXE_FILES disabled); the
      source is kept under src/osx/ for reversibility. Constructing an OSX
      driver now warns once. 'osx' remains selectable (PDLCAIRO_BACKEND=osx
      or backend => 'osx') as a legacy fallback.
    - PGPLOT layer: the /osx device (legacy) and the new /gs, /gw devices
      now display through giza_server (Driver::GS).
    - wait_all() is a harmless no-op under the gs path (empty OSX queue;
      no warning), so existing nowait+wait_all scripts keep working.
    - examples/regress_gs.pl: regression harness for the unified path
      (matplotlib-style, PGPLOT-style, show_interactive, wait_all no-op,
      gnuplot fallback).
    - API tidy-up (additive, non-breaking): added matplotlib Axes-method
      aliases set_xlim / set_ylim (set_ylim inherits the lo>hi negative-up
      reversal), set_xticks / set_yticks, and plot (alias of line). The
      existing short forms xlim / ylim / xticks / yticks remain the canonical
      implementation and are unchanged; no deprecation. set_xlim/set_ylim were
      previously missing. Removed a duplicate no-op set_tight_layout definition
      and dead commented-out ylim code in Axes.pm. New test t/06_aliases.t.
    - Added PDL::Graphics::Cairo->new(%opts) as a constructor-style alias for
      figure(); figure() remains the primary entry point.
    - README / README.ja / docs: corrected unification drift — giza_server
      ('gs') is documented as the macOS default for show(); the legacy
      osx/pdlcairo_viewer path is shown as deprecated (not the default, not
      built by make); wait_all() noted as a gs no-op; imread() fallback order
      corrected to PDL::IO::PNG -> PDL::IO::Image -> PDL::IO::Pic(rpic).

0.01  (first appear in Github, 2026-05-18)
    - Initial release
    - Backend: Cairo + Pango (PNG / PDF / SVG output)
    - Plot types: line, scatter, bar, barh, hist, errorbar,
                  fill_between, step, stem, imshow, contourf,
                  pie, axhline, axvline, axvspan, axhspan,
                  text, annotate, boxplot, violinplot, qqplot,
                  hist_kde, heatmap, stackplot, eventplot, quiver
    - Axes: autoscale, grid, legend, colorbar, twinx
    - Scale: linear, log (semilog-x/y, log-log)
    - Colormap: viridis, plasma, jet, hot, cool, gray, RdBu
    - Subplot grid: subplots(rows, cols)
    - Unicode text via Pango
    - PGPLOT compatibility layer (PDL::Graphics::Cairo::PGPLOT)
        - 53 functions fully implemented
        - cpgbox / pgbox with A/N/S/T/B/C/G/V options
        - cpgenv negative-up Y axis (ymin > ymax)
        - PGPLOT_BACKGROUND=black support
        - Multi-panel column-major layout (negative nxsub)
        - cpgmtxt multi-line title (disp parameter)
        - cpgsave / cpgunsa attribute stack
        - cpgrnd / cpgrnge / cpgnumb (untested)
    - Interactive display via gnuplot (aqua / wxt / x11)
